            },
            {
                "caption": "left: F\u2081 and F\u2082 drawn green on their lines of action (dash-dot) \u2014 the lines are NOT parallel, so they meet somewhere",
                "title": "The two given forces"
            },
            {
                "caption": "left: F\u2081 flashes \u2014 right: the same vector, drawn to scale from the start of the load line, parallel to its line of action",
                "title": "Lay off F\u2081"
            },
            {
                "caption": "left: F\u2082 flashes \u2014 right: F\u2082 continues from the tip of F\u2081, again parallel to its own line of action: the two given forces now form an open polygon",
                "title": "F\u2082 tip to tail"
            },
            {
                "caption": "left: extend both lines of action \u2014 they meet at P. Any resultant of the two forces must pass through that point, because neither force has a moment about it",
                "title": "Where do the lines cross?"
            },
